 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "For s \u2265 1, arcsin s = \u03c0/2, so sin (2 * arcsin s) = sin \u03c0 = 0, and \u221a(1 - s\u00b2) = 0 makes the right side 0; s \u2264 -1 is symmetric. Mathlib's matching `Real.cos_arcsin` (Inverse.lean:246-247) has no hypotheses, with the comment 'junk values ... make this true even outside [-1, 1]'.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Trigonometric/Arcsin.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `h\u2080` and `h\u2081` from `sin_two_mul_arcsin`; prove the out-of-range case with `arcsin_of_one_le`/`arcsin_of_le_neg_one` and `Real.sqrt_eq_zero_of_nonpos`. Keep the bounds on `sin_two_mul_arcsin_sq`, which needs them.",
   "issue": "`Real.sin_two_mul_arcsin` requires `-1 \u2264 s` and `s \u2264 1`, but the identity holds for all real `s`, so callers must prove bounds the lemma does not use.",
   "line": 32
  }
 ],
